pendell@hotmail.com wrote:
> Stats:
> 
> low strength , medium int, low-med wisdom,  low constitution, high
> dexterity, high charisma.
> 
> Concept: A bard is a traveling minstrel,  a supernatural class that
> relies on the power of music.
> 
> Schtick:
> 
> A bard always starts with a musical instrument. Remember the
> Improvise[y/n]?  command when an instrument is a)pplied?  We're about
> to expand on that.
> 
> Currently, the only effect an instrument has is when it is used at the
> drawbridge for the passtune.  Now, however, the tunes themselves have
> magical effect.   For instance, the tune AAAFG might toggle "conflict"
> on.  Play the same tune again to turn conflict off.   The tune BAADG
> may have the "aggravate monster" effect.  The tune CDDFG will "remove
> curse".  And so on.
> 
> The bard songs will be a combination of ring, amulet, scroll, or book
> effects.  Some of the effects will be quite positive (remove curse,
> scare monster for N turns) others will be negative (destroy armor,
> amnesia).
> 
> What tunes do what is randomized at the beginning of every game. Every
> bard effect is assigned to a random 5-note tune.  Two low-level songs
> will be given at game start. Others can be revealed through prayer or
> through discovering them written on scrolls or on the walls of the
> dungeon.
> 
> But 90% of bard effects are uncovered through simple experimentation --
> the bard starts plunking away at his instrument to see what tunes do
> what different things.  For instance, if he plays AAAAA and his helmet
> turns to dust and blows away, he knows not to play that again.
> 
> Playing a musical tune costs Pw, regardless of success, failure, or
> effect.
> 
> Some bard songs are affected by character level. For instance, the
> "scare monster" effect by a 1st-level bard would scare low-level
> monsters for X turns.  the same song by a 15-th level bard would
> terrify archliches for x+y turns.
> 
> Only bards can play bard songs and achieve effects with them.
> 
> Quest Leader:  The King.
> Quest Artifact/Quest Nemesis: Suggestions?
> 
> Other than that,  a bard has the same stats as a tourist. He should
> also experience a penalty when attempting to read a book, as we're
> trying to get him to depend on his songs.
> 
On a different twist to all the other suggestions:
1) add a gem to the game called a Ballybran crystal
2) musical instruments only have magical properties if this crystal is 
applied to the musical instrument by a bard
3) The quest leader is called Killashandra of the Heptite Guild. The 
quest levels are hazardous...
4) every 40,000 turns the Bard has to find a closet and weather the "storms"
5) a bard can apply a Ballybran crystal to an Elven weapon to add sonic 
damage



